course: dictionary
lesson: 7818
title: Quieten: from noise to calm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The verb quieten means to make something quieter or calmer, or to become quiet or calm yourself. The word quiet is inside it, and the ending -en often means to make or to become. «The class quietened when the head came in.» The room went from noisy to silent, so quietened means became quiet.
explain: Quieten can also mean making a person or thing calm: «She quietened the crying baby.» The baby stopped crying because of what she did. Teachers often say quieten down, as in «Quieten down, please, everyone!»
explain: Quieten can also be used for feelings and worries, not just sound. «Knowing what to do next time, like the family fire plan or the emergency number, turns "I was helpless" into "I'd know what to do", and that is one of the best ways to quieten a scary memory.» The plan does not delete the memory. It makes the fear less strong, so quieten means to make less strong here.
fact: Quieten is a verb: quieten, quietens, quietened, quietening.
fact: «Quieten» means to become quiet or calmer, or to make someone or something quiet or calm.
fact: «Quieten» can also mean to make worries or fears less strong, as in «quieten your fears».
fact: «Quieten down» is a common phrase, often said in class: «Quieten down, please.»
fact: Quieten is used in the UK, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand.
exercise: «The class quietened when the head came in.» What does quietened mean here? | Ran out of the room | Started singing loudly | Went home early | *Became quiet
exercise: «She quietened the crying baby.» What did she do? | *Calmed the baby so it was quieter | Woke the baby up | Made the baby laugh loudly | Dropped the baby's toy
exercise: Priya says, «A plan can quieten my fears.» What does quieten mean here? | Make bigger | Forget the plan | *Make less strong | Make louder
test: «Quieten down, please, everyone!» What does quieten down ask people to do? | Sing a song | Run to the door | *Become quiet | Shout louder
test: Which meaning fits «quieten your fears»? | *Make your fears less strong | Tell your fears to leave the room | Make your fears bigger | Write your fears down
exam: Which sentence uses quieten to mean make a feeling less strong? | «He quietened the loud dog.» | «Quieten the pencil case.» | «The bell quietened at noon.» | *«The bedtime story quietened her worries.»
